          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "réseau is usually traced to Old French reseuil, a small form of rets \"net\" (EtymDB has rets from Old French reiz), which goes back to Latin rēte \"a net\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
